course: dictionary
lesson: 4672
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one you need. Hole is a good example. «Birds may nest in a nest box in spring, and the size of the hole decides which birds can use it» means an opening, because the size of the hole matters.
explain: «A dog has 42 teeth and a cat has 30, and their long pointed canines make deep narrow holes that trap germs» also uses hole to mean an opening, this time a deep, narrow mark made by a bite. Read the words around hole to find the meaning.
explain: Hole can also mean a weak part or a mistake, as in a hole in a plan. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Hole» means an empty space or opening in something solid.
fact: An animal's home underground is also called a hole, such as a rabbit hole.
fact: In golf, a hole is the small place you hit the ball into.
fact: Informal: «in a hole» means in trouble.
exercise: «Watch out for holes when you run across the field.» What is a hole here? | A golf ball | *An empty opening in the ground | A rabbit's dinner | A nice place to sit
exercise: «The plan had a hole in it, so it failed.» What does hole mean here? | A piece of cheese | An animal's home | *A weak part or mistake | The place you hit a golf ball
exercise: «The rabbit ran down its hole to hide.» What does hole mean here? | A hole punch for paper | A mistake in a plan | A small golf course | *An animal's home underground
test: «Dinosaurs had legs straight under the body, which shows as a hole in the hip socket.» Which meaning of hole fits? | Informal: an unpleasant place | *An empty opening in something solid | A golf course | A weak part in a plan
test: Dad says he is «in a hole» after spending all his money. What does it mean? | In a deep pit in the garden | Hiding under the ground | Playing golf | *In trouble
exam: «Çatalhöyük ... people climbed in through holes with ladders.» What does this show about the holes? | They were animals' homes under the ground | They were mistakes in the town plan | *They were openings people could climb through | They were golf holes
